 ],
 "text": "What would happen if you got twice as rich every single day? Day 1. You have $1, you buy a pack of gum, and the guy at the corner shop doesn't even look up. Day 10. $512. You take 8 friends to dinner and pay for everyone. You've never been this popular. Day 20. $524,000. Your phone won't stop ringing, cousins you've never met want to catch up. Day 30. $537,000. You buy the building you've been renting in, your old landlord asks if you're hiring. Day 41. $1.1 trillion. You're richer than anyone alive. The bank manager walks you to the lift personally. Day 48. $140 trillion. That's more than the whole world earns in a year. Countries start calling you for a loan. Day 50. $563 trillion. You own more than all the wealth on earth. There's nothing left to buy. Day 51. Your friend still slides you the bill."
